  "structure": {
    "block_count": 49,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "Diarrhea During Pregnancy? Here’s What's Normal — and How to Ease It",
        "text_sha256": "cf0f8c5d636838eaef8ec9cb2fc17d3c395834fc457244882ff48a4b06c4ce47",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Light copy updates, updates to sourcing, and fact-checked for accuracy.",
        "text_sha256": "ce4b0fa95b50aecf6e7b67e3e57fba87415f35177add6e78e3c831eddc829533",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "diarrhea pregnancy",
        "text_sha256": "6ea4434f204b08fa53976a80cd2c83979cfb424eabe9c7547f39cd28a0cfb920",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Are you experiencing diarrhea during pregnancy? Here's everything you'll need to know, plus remedies if you find yourself visiting the bathroom too often.",
        "text_sha256": "b83ebff87aeff15cee8852de301ad8e1d1c74022e4c454ed77129d299f26e7ef",
        "word_count": 23
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "While lots of women complain about being stopped up during pregnancy, the opposite can happen too — though not as often, and it generally doesn't last as long. Medically defined as loose (or watery) and unusually frequent bowel movements, diarrhea is definitely one of those \"you'll know it if you have it\" pregnancy symptoms .",
        "text_sha256": "a2d14107e09807a2dd57aa829abb0b74db6aef06faddeef47bc7f0f8696aba74",
        "word_count": 55
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"I'm alternating between diarrhea and constipation,\" says What to Expect Community user BlueZZ. \"Don't even remember what a normal bowel movement feels like. Isn't pregnancy glorious?!\"",
        "text_sha256": "a3e58eeb8a76fc92d2e424f087d1702befcf3891850cca4de295494ef2827e2d",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Here's everything you need to know if you're experiencing diarrhea during pregnancy, including the best ways to safely treat it.",
        "text_sha256": "ac0b10bf6105008a9e2a6d3c8219310c538309cea02f01d5ada0c05187a4b385",
        "word_count": 20
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Key Takeaways",
        "text_sha256": "cc3f7f0f4513969e418b56fb93ec0876fd96dd6498395b04301f70dbddff8a45",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Diarrhea during pregnancy is less common than constipation but can happen due to diet changes, increased water intake, prenatal vitamins, or mild infections — and it can also occur right before labor as the body prepares for birth.",
        "text_sha256": "4fa0d8722322145d18a10256e8b0577e06eec7859f29f37e3bba1e4d21f7755e",
        "word_count": 38
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Treatment focuses on diet and hydration: Avoid fatty, spicy, or high-sugar foods; try gentle options like bananas, rice, and cooked vegetables; and drink plenty of water or electrolyte-rich fluids to prevent dehydration.",
        "text_sha256": "04c792f3a48a4502f96ff9a23dd107691814eb096ce4cc805931a4239826c7e1",
        "word_count": 32
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Call your doctor if symptoms persist or worsen, especially if you have more than three stools per day, diarrhea lasting over 48 hours, or signs of infection or dehydration, since these can pose risks in pregnancy.",
        "text_sha256": "3c62c557667d714524adafc703498a79dd258e3c0a6e36f7f741cb7cba3a9a24",
        "word_count": 36
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What causes diarrhea during pregnancy?",
        "text_sha256": "1eaa53b5ded414d71165287c936bd7f071acaf03613fd9f9d68fbe10c8459f45",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Unlike constipation , which can be caused by pregnancy's fluctuating hormones, diarrhea tends to be caused by something that originates outside your body — and something that's not necessarily harmful either.",
        "text_sha256": "7f4f5776c333ea77af751505187241af1049fbd988cf1b8da7d34d8b6e0abcb8",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Diarrhea may be the result of all that good-for-you food you're now eating, the extra water you're drinking, or even the workouts you've begun. It can also happen right before going to labor, as your muscles loosen and prepare for childbirth. Trusted SourceAmerican College of Obstetricians and GynecologistsProblems of the Digestive SystemSee All Sources [1]",
        "text_sha256": "ca2a08fc9e61126b98b069e8678deb74b0c22daab0bf372eb8065e889b2b7370",
        "word_count": 55
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceAmerican College of Obstetricians and GynecologistsProblems of the Digestive SystemSee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "d196862eda97104167c7ba10d4ce4e849ede9c37cc5dc352cb7b4ac9bc3420e3",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Some women find that their prenatal vitamin causes loose stools; changing brands can sometimes make all the difference.",
        "text_sha256": "7b000066e810d7641de04c6f88894d4b07117e030e689cddf12e4e7508ea1527",
        "word_count": 18
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "That said, there are things that can cause diarrhea during pregnancy that have nothing to do with hormones or lifestyle changes. Food poisoning, intestinal parasites, or a simple stomach flu may be behind a nasty bout of stomach bugs during pregnancy. If you suspect any of these might be the case, call your practitioner ASAP so you can be tested and treated. Trusted SourceNational Institutes of Health, MedlinePlusWhen you have diarrheaSee All Sources [2]",
        "text_sha256": "864ce59971dc13a77813f7ddf90f059a3b16a71ac1a2a0a99d3933845ec47e87",
        "word_count": 74
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceNational Institutes of Health, MedlinePlusWhen you have diarrheaSee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "9197756424d01123e71db90af77adf749af2b7459439ad09cd6d15d561ac38ba",
        "word_count": 11
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Remedies for diarrhea during pregnancy",
        "text_sha256": "abb5da70bb231a9b6995bf22c16b5f200256468acd0a18256e2a4a167855f9dd",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Avoid certain foods",
        "text_sha256": "87ca04ede87bc1e8b67716b175a864c958285c6ec969afad47553335dceb81c1",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Keep away from foods that could make the problem worse: dried fruits (consider prunes your enemy); fatty or spicy foods; and milk, especially if you're lactose intolerant. The so-called BRAT diet (bananas, rice, applesauce, toast) has been recommended for years because it’s gentle on your digestive system and can help make stools firmer and more solid. Trusted SourceNational Institutes of Health, MedlinePlusDiarrheaSee All Sources [3]",
        "text_sha256": "4058dfdc910d69af73dc85f8d59941fb216857039af5dd5684aed96695cc8613",
        "word_count": 65
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceNational Institutes of Health, MedlinePlusDiarrheaSee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "cbebe440f70c091f7011393827d2b40adc1a8c28847653e175a81fa86c26eb8a",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "However, the newest thinking expands on those options to include other important vitamins and minerals (especially zinc) that are not provided by the BRAT diet. Trusted SourceNational Institutes of Health, Office of Dietary SupplementsZincSee All Sources [4] Try adding the following:",
        "text_sha256": "8c2b3b68881596df85dfc9ced0df70f72c035b4bd4628982d332a3f0270321fc",
        "word_count": 41
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceNational Institutes of Health, Office of Dietary SupplementsZincSee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "8ff414f0989fca96c3cad4405b931aceca159e9e5663026f9f4ea3f34584b76a",
        "word_count": 11
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Other starchy foods like potatoes, unsweetened cereals, and crackers",
        "text_sha256": "fc7309a3cd8c12506e11efd0527f0749087674505c945e8632cc7939e6bca5a4",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Cooked vegetables including carrots, peeled zucchini, green beans, beets, and acorn squash",
        "text_sha256": "c3f1d8ebcdbda99dc98234a8a8ddf8e7e9f372edaa34999870699791da22c580",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000026",
        "block_index": 26,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Non-milk-based soups with vegetables",
        "text_sha256": "53f80fbf288af745143b5f38fdcf4a0dd53634c21c5c1a6c4e755b6afe030dda",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000027",
        "block_index": 27,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Lean meats",
        "text_sha256": "b69bd14658bb08fd982aefed77575b69b88b225a9bc801c9818dc80c57107068",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000028",
        "block_index": 28,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Cooked eggs",
        "text_sha256": "e80aa5283b7bee6cdcd0283e13fc6e7833523b47d550ab141745aa57b2e15070",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000029",
        "block_index": 29,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Yogurt, especially with live, active cultures of lactobacillus acidophilus",
        "text_sha256": "23e336ce37f090303e171865f8c23f300ebf4aa9548be170256bf8046faad45c",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000030",
        "block_index": 30,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Also be sure to avoid eating a few foods that can make diarrhea worse:",
        "text_sha256": "058447269dc20d4d17fe8a4055ca7a75fc855e3f1c5f3b17c4241f74d317e445",
        "word_count": 14
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000031",
        "block_index": 31,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "\"Simple\" high-sugar drinks (apple and grape juice, gelatin, regular colas, and other soft drinks), which can draw water into your tummy, making diarrhea last even longer",
        "text_sha256": "c20c2ce6e3bef4b729a8eb34b3d37c0c8fb1478c48922ab228237c746031f869",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000032",
        "block_index": 32,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Fatty and fried foods",
        "text_sha256": "f3a32beae6e2a26baa7ccea6f6945a59321230d065726264c29a556bf0f6266e",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000033",
        "block_index": 33,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Gas-causing fruits and vegetables, such as beans, broccoli, peas, prunes, and chickpeas",
        "text_sha256": "bbb66e7f215a758f5f54adc554d001cc4d46f0664ee98ed80ec08163d62e2800",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000034",
        "block_index": 34,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Dairy products, if they're causing gas or other intestinal upset",
        "text_sha256": "d4107b2ba8a551734e976c399e8a2cac8cb4041af04ba97917b6cd7d992dbfa5",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000035",
        "block_index": 35,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Drink plenty of water",
        "text_sha256": "755aae0d584950ea60d0b61189bb2bfea1d187384c6814f8685d03bf1751a130",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000036",
        "block_index": 36,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Also key? Staying hydrated — which is important throughout your pregnancy, but especially when diarrhea strikes. The recommended amount varies based on your body type and size, and how active you are, but aim for eight to 10 8-ounce glasses of water (from all sources) a day.",
        "text_sha256": "66647e797343fbe9bb1874a9ddd9d9254f37b6ccc408da62620e24ff2b58ba24",
        "word_count": 47
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000037",
        "block_index": 37,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Ask your doctor about sipping a sports drink with electrolytes, which can replenish lost fluids plus key minerals like sodium, chloride and potassium.",
        "text_sha256": "38684e9eabe215593e4499c9aba2f7176622567f5dcb42929c5d6fda9aa39b03",
        "word_count": 23
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000038",
        "block_index": 38,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Ask about medications",
        "text_sha256": "a35ecdaa5ed83ee1be16022ed24d13e1b9a3055e04c8db0a128c3028893f2dd1",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000039",
        "block_index": 39,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Always check with your doctor before taking any over-the-counter diarrhea medications. And of course, if you’re on a stool softener for constipation in pregnancy, be sure to stop taking it until your stools return to a normal consistency.",
        "text_sha256": "20e2a22b2a98540c3fedac7ed104ff3159124a9b6e675e0fe97a8a542e98d248",
        "word_count": 38
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000040",
        "block_index": 40,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "When to call your doctor",
        "text_sha256": "0a749c1d09ff9584d48653560b068b92eb32ffe8cfbc2b38f79705921edd8309",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000041",
        "block_index": 41,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Remember, while a mild case of diarrhea isn't anything to really worry about during pregnancy, there are a few times you should get in touch with your practitioner right away, including if you:",
        "text_sha256": "fb160d4e5ce8076c8b9a9ad20a8bdfc18468701101cbfbb70afd55d0cbe62028",
        "word_count": 33
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000042",
        "block_index": 42,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Have more than three stools a day",
        "text_sha256": "a4231ac747db97e4a50bb9ec753126ce5992d0ddb960c6694552e012416bfa3d",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000043",
        "block_index": 43,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Have diarrhea lasting more than 48 hours, despite dietary changes",
        "text_sha256": "59e500df414b3a764f0612565a0d960f9d7248d70425c614c22a88e3c21165a1",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000044",
        "block_index": 44,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Have stools that are bloody, contain mucus, or are purely liquid",
        "text_sha256": "2c57bb21d81c4ed19b4e08c4ece4ce12f02df21dca24ab6f4a24ef1f8398cb6e",
        "word_count": 11
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000045",
        "block_index": 45,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Were recently in close contact with someone known to have a parasite or stomach flu",
        "text_sha256": "680b6c6d463a4968780718fb35d8480bd09987f71b974c08d1c35d06ef7af401",
        "word_count": 15
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000046",
        "block_index": 46,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Suspect that your diarrhea is a sign that you’re in labor",
        "text_sha256": "94e4dcc78d0838e1bf8114bd55448e8f85a0119964f752a255d0989c61aad306",
        "word_count": 11
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000047",
        "block_index": 47,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "You can also keep track of symptoms like diarrhea throughout your pregnancy using the My Journal tool in the What to Expect app , plus get tips for managing other frustrating pregnancy symptoms.",
        "text_sha256": "b6d52ce261e9c957e6a69ce381080d3771a114ae436132315d136ed3072ae490",
        "word_count": 33
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000048",
        "block_index": 48,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Diarrhea that persists for more than a couple of days, no matter how mild, is worth a call to your practitioner: It’s not only a pain in the rear, but it can also quickly lead to dehydration, a major risk factor for premature labor . For that reason alone, if you've got it, take it seriously.",
        "text_sha256": "2665f31feeb7c0c2ee8e65cafac923190d8235112e86e2912b5015b123ffdd1e",
        "word_count": 56
      }
    ],
